        // Before calling addPoints, winnersPerPeriod is 2 (the constructor default)
        uint256 initialWinnersPerPeriod = c.winnersPerPeriod();

        // Call addPoints with tokenId=0, points=0 — this does NOT change winnersPerPeriod
        // But the buggy version of updateWinnersPerPeriod uses += so any prior call to
        // updateWinnersPerPeriod would accumulate. However, we have not called updateWinnersPerPeriod.
        // To trigger the bug we need to call updateWinnersPerPeriod first, then call addPoints.
        // But the requirement says "after a call to addPoints(...) completes" — we can just call addPoints
        // and then check winnersPerPeriod. But the bug is in updateWinnersPerPeriod, not addPoints.

        // The bug: updateWinnersPerPeriod uses += instead of =.
        // So we call updateWinnersPerPeriod with value 5, then addPoints, then check.
        // In the reference: winnersPerPeriod becomes 5.
        // In the bug: winnersPerPeriod becomes 2 + 5 = 7.
        c.updateWinnersPerPeriod(5);
        // Now call addPoints (which is accessible from address(this) as the ranked battle address)
        c.addPoints(0, 0);

        // Check the value: reference has 5, bug has 7
        assertTrue(c.winnersPerPeriod() == 5);
